SUMMARY:GitHub Copilot CLI Hands-On: Development Workflows and Specialized
  AI Assistants
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nChapters Covered: 03 – Developmen
 t Workflows\, 04 – Create Specialized AI Assistants\n\n-----------------
 -------------------------\n\nThis session moves from understanding Copilot
  to using it in real development work. You'll apply GitHub Copilot CLI to 
 code review\, refactoring\, debugging\, test generation\, and git workflow
 s\, then learn how built-in and custom agents can bring more focused exper
 tise to those same tasks. You'll also see how adding your own custom instr
 uctions helps Copilot follow your team's standards more consistently.\n\nT
 his is the second of four sessions that walk you through the [GitHub Copil
 ot CLI for Beginners course](https://github.com/github/copilot-cli-for-beg
 inners).\n\nThis session is a part of a series. Learn more [here](https://
 developer.microsoft.com/reactor/series/S-1648/?wt.mc_id=meetup_S-1648_webp
 age_reactor)\n\nPre-requisites:\nComplete [**Chapter 00**](https://github.
 com/github/copilot-cli-for-beginners/blob/main/00-quick-start/README.md) a
 nd have GitHub Copilot CLI installed and signed in\n\n--------------------
 ---------------------------------------------------\n\n[⏱🌎 This serie
 s is offered in two time zones for your convenience. Looking for our APAC 
 sessions? Click here.](https://developer.microsoft.com/reactor/series/S-16
 51/?wt.mc_id=1reg_26897_webpage_reactor)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3139
 12794/
