SUMMARY:GitHub Copilot CLI Hands-On: Using AI Skills to Automate Repeatabl
 e Work
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nChapters Covered: 05 – Automate R
 epetitive Tasks\n\n------------------------------------------\n\nIn this s
 ession\, you'll learn how to use Copilot CLI to automate repeatable work b
 y using skills - natural language descriptions of workflows and processes.
  Learn what skills are\, where you can access a library of skills to use i
 n your projects\, and how skills can be used by Copilot CLI.\n\nThis is th
 e third of four sessions that walk you through the [GitHub Copilot CLI for
  Beginners course](https://github.com/github/copilot-cli-for-beginners).\n
 \nThis session is a part of a series. Learn more [here](https://developer.
 microsoft.com/reactor/series/S-1648/?wt.mc_id=meetup_S-1648_webpage_reacto
 r)\n\nPre-requisites:\nComplete [**Chapter 00**](https://github.com/github
 /copilot-cli-for-beginners/blob/main/00-quick-start/README.md) and have Gi
 tHub Copilot CLI installed and signed in\n\n------------------------------
 -----------------------------------------\n\n[⏱🌎 This series is offer
 ed in two time zones for your convenience. Looking for our APAC sessions? 
 Click here.](https://developer.microsoft.com/reactor/series/S-1651/?wt.mc_
 id=1reg_26904_webpage_reactor)
